AtumModuleFactory_Create
├── when the caller is not the factory owner
│   ├── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
│   ├── it should revert even for the PaymentRails owner
│   └── it should leave the registry empty
├── when owner is zero address
│   └── it should revert with AtumModuleFactory_ZeroOwner
├── when paymentRails is zero address
│   └── it should revert with AtumModuleFactory_ZeroPaymentRails
├── when keeper is zero address
│   └── it should revert with AtumModuleFactory_ZeroKeeper
├── when paymentRails has no code
│   └── it should revert with AtumModuleFactory_PaymentRailsNotContract
├── when paymentRails was not deployed by PaymentRailsFactory
│   ├── when it is a lookalike exposing owner()
│   │   └── it should revert with AtumModuleFactory_UnknownPaymentRails
│   └── when it is a real PaymentRails deployed directly
│       └── it should revert with AtumModuleFactory_UnknownPaymentRails
└── when the caller is the factory owner and params are valid
    ├── it should deploy a new AtumModule contract
    ├── it should set the owner on the deployed module
    ├── it should not require the caller to own the PaymentRails
    ├── it should wire the module to the PaymentRails
    ├── it should set the keeper on the deployed module
    ├── it should wire the module to the factory permit2
    ├── it should register the module in the factory
    ├── it should increment the module count
    ├── it should register the module under the PaymentRails lookup
    ├── it should emit an AtumModuleCreated event carrying the keeper
    └── when called multiple times
        ├── it should deploy distinct instances
        ├── it should register all instances
        └── it should accumulate instances in the PaymentRails lookup
